.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-UNSET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-unset - Remove one environment variable


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env unset <name> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove one environment variable

.PP
Delete one ENV name from the selected personal, team, or host scope. The confirmation code confirms removal. Authorized devices receive refreshed encrypted layers with the deleted value omitted; running processes retain their environment.

.PP
ENV values are encrypted before they leave the client. The interactive picker separates shared Team globals, your private member globals, and device overrides in the active workspace; commands select exact scopes explicitly; list output shows metadata rather than secret values. Unlock the local vault when a key operation requires it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	six-character confirmation code from the preview

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for unset

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print redacted JSON metadata

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	Private device override in the active workspace; omitted uses your global values

.PP
\fB--team\fP=""
	team scope; cannot be combined with --machine


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env(1)\fP
